---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_DESC, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { VALUE } from '../../content/home';
import { KIT as K } from '../../lib/kit';
import { others } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { profilePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('about', lang);
const title = 'Fly Pet Rules 2026: Who Publishes These Pet Travel Tools';
const description = 'Fly Pet Rules in 2026: who publishes these pet travel calculators, the CDC, USDA and airline documents behind them, and why the site sells nothing to owners.';
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[profilePageSchema({ path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>About Fly Pet Rules</h1>
    <p>{AUTHOR_DESC.en}</p>
    <h2>Why these pet travel tools exist</h2>
    <p>Someone flying with a dog asks three plain questions: what the airline charges, whether the carrier fits, and what papers the trip needs, going and coming back. The pages that answer are blog lists that earn a commission on carriers and often disagree on the fee, pet shippers that want a quote request, and government pages written for veterinarians.</p>
    <p>{VALUE}</p>
    <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
    <p>The site is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that builds calculators on public data. It is an independent site, not an airline, a veterinarian, a pet shipper or a government agency. It sells nothing, takes no commission, carries no affiliate link and asks for no contact details.</p>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>What it relies on</h2>
    <p>The CDC dog import rules and its list of {K.HR.length} high-risk countries; the USDA APHIS pages for Mexico, Canada, France and the European Union, Great Britain, Japan and the tapeworm countries, with the APHIS endorsement fee schedule; and the pet pages or contracts of carriage of Delta, American, Southwest, Alaska and Frontier. Everything was read on {K.day(K.P.retrieved_at)}.</p>
    <h2>What it leaves out</h2>
    <p set:html={others()} />
    <p>Hawaiian Airlines, whose pet pages now sit on Alaska’s site, is not covered either. Veterinary advice of any kind, vet prices, pet shipper quotes and the entry rules of Hawaii, which the state sets itself. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> lists every simplification and the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> explains corrections.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, for a fee that changed or a rule we read wrong. We answer questions about a figure or a source, not about your own trip, which your airline and your accredited veterinarian decide.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
